ctober 2026 \n The Governing Council today decided to keep the three key ECB interest rates unchanged.","next_action":"Hold signalled"},"evidence":[{"q":"The increased magnitude and duration of the energy shock, as well as the implications for indirect and second-round effects, are likely to drive up inflation and lower growth.","para":2,"dir":"hawk","w":2.0,"theme":"inflation","cond":false},{"q":"Financing conditions have tightened since the Governing Council’s last meeting, which is likely to weigh on inflation and growth.","para":2,"dir":"hawk","w":2.0,"theme":"guidance","cond":false},{"q":"Energy prices have continued to rise, posing upside risks to the inflation outlook and downside risks to the growth outlook.","para":2,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"inflation","cond":false}],"baseline":{},"confidence":{"level":"Medium","why":["short text","few scored sentences"]}},{"id":"847a7abc2726","bank":"fed","title":"Federal Reserve issues FOMC statement","type":"statement","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20261028a.htm","published_at":"2026-10-28T18:00:00+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-29T14:02:15.675465+00:00","hash":"7da5fa1a55f3d46d","version":1,"words":346,"source_type":"official","transcript_status":"official","speaker":"Committee","voting_status":"NOT_APPLICABLE","score":6.2,"label":"HAWKISH","themes":{"inflation":2.0,"employment":1.0,"growth":1.0,"financial":0.0,"guidance":1.0},"hawk_n":5.0,"dove_n":0.0,"guidance":{"direction":"none","conditional":false,"quote":"","next_action":"No explicit forward guidance"},"evidence":[{"q":"While uncertainty remains elevated owing, in part, to geopolitical developments, domestic spending has been resilient.","para":17,"dir":"hawk","w":2.0,"theme":"employment","cond":false},{"q":"Productivity growth is strong, and capital investment is robust.","para":17,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"growth","cond":false},{"q":"Inflation remains elevated.","para":18,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"inflation","cond":false},{"q":"Hammack, who preferred to raise the target range for the federal funds rate by 1/4 percentage point at this meeting.","para":19,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"guidance","cond":false}],"baseline":{"institution":{"score":6.2,"date":"2026-09-16","title":"Federal Reserve issues FOMC statement","change":0.0}},"confidence":{"level":"Medium","why":["short text"]}},{"id":"23d46987719e","bank":"ecb","title":"Piero Cipollone: Interview with Milano Finanza","type":"interview","url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu//press/inter/date/2026/html/ecb.in261024~ee2ba73cf3.en.html","published_at":"2026-10-24T06:00:00+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-29T14:02:15.675465+00:00","hash":"fe49d0c105d1d698","version":1,"words":2123,"source_type":"official","transcript_status":"official","speaker":"Cipollone","voting_status":"UNKNOWN","score":2.5,"label":"LEANING HAWKISH","themes":{"inflation":0.0,"employment":0.0,"growth":0.0,"financial":0.0,"guidance":1.0},"hawk_n":1.0,"dove_n":0.0,"guidance":{"direction":"hold","conditional":false,"quote":"Will there be a limit on holdings of digital euro? \n Yes, but there won’t be limits on payments.","next_action":"Hold signalled"},"evidence":[{"q":"The digital euro will introduce a European alternative that will increase competition and, thanks to the caps on costs laid down by law, will help to reduce fees for those with less bargaining power.","para":18,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"guidance","cond":false}],"baseline":{},"confidence":{"level":"Medium","why":["few scored sentences","thin speaker baseline"]}},{"id":"8bd67b451c42","bank":"boe","title":"Physical shocks and economic resilience: a central bank perspective − speech by James Talbot","type":"speech","url":"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/speech/2026/october/physical-shocks-and-economic-resilience-speech-by-james-talbot","published_at":"2026-10-23T09:00:00+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-29T14:02:15.675465+00:00","hash":"e55fbfeff5e4906b","version":1,"words":4717,"source_type":"official","transcript_status":"official","speaker":"James Talbot","voting_status":"UNKNOWN","score":7.5,"label":"HAWKISH","themes":{"inflation":9.5,"employment":1.0,"growth":0.0,"financial":0.0,"guidance":11.0},"hawk_n":23.5,"dove_n":2.0,"guidance":{"direction":"none","conditional":false,"quote":"","next_action":"No explicit forward guidance"},"evidence":[{"q":"They can weaken demand and confidence among economic agents, tighten credit conditions and raise uncertainty.","para":20,"dir":"hawk","w":2.0,"theme":"guidance","cond":false},{"q":"Scenarios can complement the central forecast by helping us explore precisely the kinds of uncertainty I have described today: whether a shock proves temporary or persistent; whether supply or demand effects dominate; and whether initial price increases generate material second-round effects.","para":54,"dir":"hawk","w":2.0,"theme":"inflation","cond":false},{"q":"I’ll talk today about how the physical impacts of climate change can affect the economy in the near term; how we diagnose their magnitude, persistence and propagation; whether their effects belong in the central forecast or in the risks around it; and how that diagnosis informs monetary policy judgements.","para":15,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"inflation","cond":false},{"q":"I will argue that these two horizons are connected: The resilience an economy has built determines the scale and persistence of the macroeconomic impact of a shock over the monetary-policy horizon.","para":17,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"inflation","cond":false},{"q":"Without effective mitigation and adaptation, economies may therefore become less resilient over time, with the same physical hazard generating increasingly persistent effects on output, inflation, credit and public finances.","para":61,"dir":"dove","w":1.0,"theme":"inflation","cond":true},{"q":"Learning about earnings: Can we rely on labour market slack to mitigate the latest supply shock? − speech...","para":137,"dir":"dove","w":1.0,"theme":"employment","cond":false}],"baseline":{},"confidence":{"level":"Medium","why":["thin speaker baseline"]}},{"id":"c460cd7ebd31","bank":"boe","title":"The PRA’s second decade − speech by Katharine Braddick","type":"speech","url":"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/speech/2026/october/katharine-braddick-mansion-house-city-regulators-dinner-london","published_at":"2026-10-22T20:00:00+00:00","fetched_at":"2026-10-29T14:02:15.675465+00:00","hash":"b7d4b448debb4b50","version":1,"words":1755,"source_type":"official","transcript_status":"official","speaker":"Katharine Braddick","voting_status":"UNKNOWN","score":4.4,"label":"LEANING HAWKISH","themes":{"inflation":0.0,"employment":1.0,"growth":0.0,"financial":0.0,"guidance":3.0},"hawk_n":5.0,"dove_n":1.0,"guidance":{"direction":"none","conditional":false,"quote":"","next_action":"No explicit forward guidance"},"evidence":[{"q":"Security threats increase, exacerbated by a more fractured geopolitical landscape.","para":6,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"guidance","cond":false},{"q":"Interconnected financial vulnerabilities are arising from stretched sectoral valuations, rising sovereign debt levels and increased market leverage.","para":6,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"guidance","cond":false},{"q":"We will significantly increase our focus on firms’ operational and cyber resilience.","para":10,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"guidance","cond":false},{"q":"We will ensure the financial sector remains resilient to the increasingly volatile environment we now face.","para":23,"dir":"hawk","w":1.0,"theme":"employment","cond":false},{"q":"Learning about earnings: Can we rely on labour market slack to mitigate the latest supply shock? − speech...","para":33,"dir":"dove","w":1.0,"theme":"employment","cond":false}],"baseline":{},"confidence":{"level":"Medium","why":["thin speaker baseline"]}},{"id":"18ada448671f","bank":"ecb","title":"Frank Elderson: Interview with Die Presse","type":"interview","url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu//press/inter/date/2026/h